<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Hernici</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.) · capital Anagnia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Italic people of the Sacco valley in southern Latium, long-time allies of Rome whose towns are known for their massive polygonal walls.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Hernici lived in the hills of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacco-river">Sacco</a> valley, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latins">Latins</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volsci">Volsci</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aequi">Aequi</a>. Their name was explained from a Marsic word for rocks. They were an Italic people, probably related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabellians">Sabellians</a>, organised by the 5th century BCE in a league of towns centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anagni">Anagnia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their towns, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anagni">Anagnia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferentino">Ferentinum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alatri">Aletrium</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veroli">Verulae</a>, met in league councils at the Maritime Circus near Anagnia. Aletrium's acropolis with its huge polygonal walls is among the best preserved in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Wedged between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/volsci">Volsci</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aequi">Aequi</a>, the Hernici made a treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latins</a>, traditionally in 486 BCE, and fought alongside them for much of the 5th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Relations broke down in the 4th century. In 306 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anagni">Anagnia</a> led a revolt and was punished with citizenship without the vote, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferentino">Ferentinum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alatri">Aletrium</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veroli">Verulae</a>, which stayed loyal, kept their independence as allies. All became Roman municipia after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 600 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:47.76%;width:5.85%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 306 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Anagnia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hernican polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hernican</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hernican League</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-453&amp;focus=hernici" aria-label="Hernici on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5000 691 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hernici lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5320 947L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5320 947h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5320 947h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Anagnia. <a href="/atlas?year=-453&amp;focus=hernici">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

